    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Impacto de mis publicaciones\"\ndate: 10 Jun 2024\nupdate-date: 6 Aug 2026\neditor_options: \n  chunk_output_type: console\nexecute: \n  echo: false\nformat:\n  html:\n    code-tools: \n      source: true\n      caption: \"Código para cálculos y figuras\"\n---\n\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\nExisten muchas formas de medir el impacto de nuestras actividades científicas. Algunas iniciativas se basan en indicadores cuantitativos derivados de contadores y estadísticas de uso de varias redes sociales y académicas. \n\nUno de los más famosos proveedores es PlumX. \n\nPlumX registra varios indicadores del uso e impacto de publicaciones. La descripción de las cinco categorías principales se encuentra aquí:  <https://plumanalytics.com/learn/about-metrics/>.\n\nLos valores totales obtenidos para mi lista de publicaciones son los siguientes:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n| capture| citation| mention| socialMedia| usage|\n|-------:|--------:|-------:|-----------:|-----:|\n|    4562|     1400|     210|         861|  3915|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\nPero probablemente sea más informativa una presentación gráfica por publicación:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](impact_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-8-1.png){width=864}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Impacto social\n\nUna forma de medir el impacto social es considerando las citas que reciben los artículos científicos en documentos de normativas y políticas nacionales o globales. \n\nEsta es el total de mis publicaciones que tienen citas en algún instrumento de políticas globales, según los valores registrados por PlumX.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"datatables html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-550ff452a9aa700eb482\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-550ff452a9aa700eb482\">{\"x\":{\"filter\":\"none\",\"vertical\":false,\"data\":[[19],[218]],\"container\":\"<table class=\\\"display\\\">\\n  <thead>\\n    <tr>\\n      <th>Total documents<\\/th>\\n      <th>Total policy citations<\\/th>\\n    <\\/tr>\\n  <\\/thead>\\n<\\/table>\",\"options\":{\"columnDefs\":[{\"className\":\"dt-right\",\"targets\":[0,1]},{\"name\":\"Total documents\",\"targets\":0},{\"name\":\"Total policy citations\",\"targets\":1}],\"order\":[],\"autoWidth\":false,\"orderClasses\":false}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\nEn la siguiente tabla presento una lista detallada de estas publicaciones con los enlaces a sus perfiles en PlumX.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"datatables html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-9145ec93ec63d5d0553a\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-9145ec93ec63d5d0553a\">{\"x\":{\"filter\":\"none\",\"vertical\":false,\"data\":[[\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biocon.2013.07.032'>Using limited data to detect changes in species distributions: Insights from Amazon parrots in Venezuela<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biocon.2020.108834'>Myanmar's terrestrial ecosystems: Status, threats and conservation opportunities<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecolind.2024.111790'>Trade-Offs in the Use of Direct and Indirect Indicators of Ecosystem Degradation for Risk Assessment<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1016/j.prevetmed.2016.11.023'>One Health proof of concept: Bringing a transdisciplinary approach to surveillance for zoonotic viruses at the human-wild animal interface<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1017/s0030605323001771'>First Red List of Ecosystems assessment of a tropical glacier ecosystem to diagnose the pathways toward imminent collapse<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1038/s41559-023-02320-5'>Beyond the headline: roles of the Red List of Ecosystems in implementing the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05318-4'>A function-based typology for Earth’s ecosystems<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1111/cobi.13995'>Effects of interactions between anthropogenic stressors and recurring perturbations on ecosystem resilience and collapse<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1111/cobi.14169'>Contributions of Red Lists of Ecosystems to risk-based design and management of protected and conserved areas in Africa<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1111/conl.12623'>An ecosystem risk assessment of temperate and tropical forests of the Americas with an outlook on future conservation strategies<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1111/conl.12666'>Impacts of the IUCN Red List of Ecosystems on conservation policy and practice<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1111/conl.12680'>Ecosystem indices to support global biodiversity conservation<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1186/s42522-021-00036-9'>Socializing One Health: an innovative strategy to investigate social and behavioral risks of emerging viral threats<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0063570'>Congruence and Diversity of Butterfly-Host Plant Associations at Higher Taxonomic Levels<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0110236'>Evaluation of Local Media Surveillance for Improved Disease Recognition and Monitoring in Global Hotspot Regions<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.2305/cjdf9122'>{Guidelines for the application of IUCN Red List of Ecosystems Categories and Criteria: version 2.0}<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.2305/cppc6126'>{Standards, methods and guidelines for cross-referencing ecosystem classifications and maps to the IUCN Global Ecosystem Typology}<\\/a>\",\"<a href='https://doi.org/10.2305/iucn.